          %h2#notation Notation
          %p
            An enlargement of a specific category, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %p
            As a notation for the operation on a general category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇑
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow C
            has been proposed.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p Since the enlargement is not well-specified by the above intuitive description, there are several different definitions, which are often equivalent but not always.
          %p
            Henceforth we fix two universes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
