                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}\in \mathbf{V}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %em small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %em large
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
            (or in the next larger universe
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{W}
            = succeed "." do
              %em very large
          %h3#models_of_a_theory Models of a theory
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            of some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇑
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow C
            to be the category of large
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            of the same theory. For instance:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+sets"} small sets
                is the category of small models of the theory with one sort and no operations or relations. The category of large models of this theory is just the very large category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SET
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SET
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+set"} large sets
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, from categories such as
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                of small
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi GRP
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GRP
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CAT
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TOP
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TOP
                of large groups, categories, and topological spaces.
          %p
            Note that the theory could be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theory"} essentially algebraic
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher-order+logic"} higher-order
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed "." do
              %strong logical enlargement
            %em any
            large category.
          %h3#LocallyPresentableEnlargement Locally presentable enlargement
          %p
            For any large category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SET
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},SET]
            contains
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SET
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},SET]
            is
            = succeed "-bicomplete," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SET
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SET
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            was
            = succeed "-complete" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SET
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow [C^{op},SET]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
            all limits that exist in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            However, it hardly preserves any
            %em colimits
            (since it is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            which preserves some class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            of colimits in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SET
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},SET]
            consisting of the presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi SET
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}\to SET
            which preserved limit the colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            (i.e. take them to limits in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SET
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SET
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⇑
                      %mi Φ
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            preserve all limits, the Yoneda embedding of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            factors through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⇑
                      %mi Φ
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            are preserved by this restricted embedding.
          %p
            Moreover,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⇑
                    %mi Φ
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C
            is closed under limits in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SET
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},SET]
            = succeed "-complete." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SET
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SET
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            are at most
            = succeed "," do
              %em large
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⇑
                    %mi Φ
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C
            is reflective in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SET
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},SET]
            = succeed "-cocomplete." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SET
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SET
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %em small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is the class of all small colimits existing in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            We will refer to this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⇑
                    %mi Φ
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C
            as the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong locally presentable enlargement
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            relative to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
            = succeed "-presentable," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            of the first universe
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi Cts
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda Cts(A,B)
            denotes the category of
            = succeed "-small-limit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is locally presentable relative to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              and a small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi λ
                      %mi Cts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\simeq \lambda Cts(A^{op},Set)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              denotes the class of all small colimits in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⇑
                        %mi Φ
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi λ
                      %mi Cts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SET
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C \simeq \lambda Cts(A^{op},SET)
          %p
            Note that in this case,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi Cts
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SET
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda Cts(A^{op},SET)
            is the category of large models of the theory (namely
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the category of small ones. Thus, the theorem says that when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is locally presentable, the locally presentable enlargement is the same as the logical one.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Write
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi λ
                      %mi Cts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SET
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C' \coloneqq \lambda Cts(A^{op},SET)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\hookrightarrow C'
            %p
              Now every object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a small colimit of objects of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              are all
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is the size of the universe
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              is locally
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is closed under small colimits in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              is locally
              = succeed "-presentable," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed "-presentable," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi κ
                      %mi Cts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SET
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C' \simeq \kappa Cts(C^{op},SET)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mi Cts
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SET
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa Cts(C^{op},SET)
              is precisely
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⇑
                        %mi Φ
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Uparrow_\Phi C
          %p
            However, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not locally presentable, then its logical and locally-presentable enlargements can disagree. In fact, they will
            %em usually
            disagree in this case, since if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not locally presentable relative to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
            either, whereas its locally-presentable enlargement is, by definition, locally presentable relative to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{V}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            are quite different.
          %h3#accessible_enlargement Accessible enlargement
          %p
            There is a simple modification of the locally-presentable enlargement which makes it agree with the logical enlargement for all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+categories"} accessible categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mi Cts
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SET
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa Cts(C^{op},SET)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mi Flat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SET
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa Flat(C^{op},SET)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functors"} flat functors
            (functors that “would preserve all
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %strong accessible enlargement
          %p
            Essentially the same proof as for the theorem above shows that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is accessible relative to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{U}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi λ
                    %mi Flat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\simeq \lambda Flat(A^{op},Set)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mi Flat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SET
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda Flat(A^{op},SET)
          %p
            Note that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has all small limits, then its accessible and locally-presentable enlargements are the same, since a functor defined on a category with
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-continuous" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-flat." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            does not have small limits, then its locally-presentable enlargement
            %em does
            have all large limits, whereas its accessible enlargement does not.
          %p
            Thus, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is “poorly behaved,” its accessible enlargement is “closer to it” (in particular, identical to its logical enlargement if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is accessible) and thus equally poorly behaved, whereas its locally-presentable enlargement is further from it, but better behaved (complete and cocomplete). For some purposes one may want one of these behaviors; for other purposes one may want the other.
          %h3#monoidal_enlargements Monoidal enlargements
          %p
            One may further ask for an enlargement which inherits whatever additional structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has, such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            theorem implies that when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is monoidal, so is its locally-presentable enlargement—and moreover, the latter is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            even if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not!
